hello this is Steve Kaufman  welcome to the linguist what is the  linguist it's a resource for language  learning I believe that people can speak  more than one language they can enjoy  doing it they can have fun learning I  believe the world will be a better place  if we all speak more than one language I  speak ten languages now some are Asian  languages some are European languages  Germanic languages Slavic languages  Romance languages and it gives me  tremendous satisfaction happiness as  well as social and even professional  advantages along the way I've discovered  how to most effectively learn languages  and the biggest thing is to simply have  fun and enjoy it avoid the complicated  grammar explanations and exercises and  worksheets that we associate with  traditional language learning in schools  what you need to do is to find content  to listen to and to read which you enjoy  which you have chosen and which is more  or less at your level just a little bit  difficult for you and so here at the  linguist we have lots of content like  that that you can choose and the number  of items we have in our library is  constantly growing a lot of it is  contributed by members of the linguist  community you have to listen a lot you  have to read a lot and you have to focus  mostly on words not on rules of grammar  yes just words how they work what they  mean how they work with other words and  all of the functionality that you need  to do that effectively you will find at  our related website which is called link  and there we keep track of the words as  you are learning them so you actually  find out how many words you know we help  you find content that is at your level  and then we give you a lot of tools  to practice with your words and and to  develop phrases that you can then save  from these words and that is really all  you need to do endure yourself and work  on words now this also is true when you  speak and write you don't need to feel  any pressure to speak and write but most  of us after we have listened and read  and accumulated a lot of words we want  to say something in the language we  don't necessarily want people to correct  us all the time but we want to be  improving as we use the language and  that is again a feature at link where we  emphasize the different ways in which  you can take the words that you are  learning and use them in your writing  and speaking and then when you go to  write and speak when you for whatever  reason don't use the words properly or  the way they're used by the native  speaker then we encourage you to take  these words and bring them into your  link system and work with them and study  them no further detailed information on  how to use link is available at the link  website here we just want you to browse  around see the content that we have in  our library for whatever language you're  interested in understand our philosophy  of language learning the importance of  enjoyment the importance of learning  words and when you feel like it go visit  that link you can register free of  charge and use the functionality that we  have there or you can also enroll for  discussions with the tutor or you can  write and have your writing corrected so  there's a whole world of language  learning awaiting you at link and you  will also there meet the rest of the  link community all around the world  people who are learning languages who  are helping each other learn languages  who are creating original and and  delightful content in their own native  language that other members of the  linked community are using in order to  learn those languages so it's an  exciting new world it's a different  approach to language learning it's that  one that we think is fun  and brings people together from many  many different cultures so thank you for  visiting us and please take the time to  look around
 

